<section id="compound" class="section">
  {# Split, reversed: statement left, the agent's compounding memory right.
     Pills swap three static views of the SAME agent: learnings, skills,
     context. Same data-swap mechanic as #parallel; JS-off shows Learnings
     settled. Team-taught learnings carry the teammate's avatar. #}
  <div class="split split-rev reveal">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <h2 class="sec-title">Teach once. Better forever.</h2>
      <p class="split-line">Correct an agent once and it sticks, for everyone. Every learning, skill, and file it carries belongs to the whole team.</p>
      <p class="split-line">That's compounding: each week your agents know your business better than the last.</p>
      <p class="split-line">New people inherit it all on day one, and nothing walks out the door.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="split-visual">
      <div class="feat-demo" data-swap-group="feat">
        <div class="chat-tabs feat-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="What the agent carries">
          <button class="chat-tab active" data-swap="0" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Learnings</button>
          <button class="chat-tab" data-swap="1" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Skills</button>
          <button class="chat-tab" data-swap="2" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Context</button>
        </div>

